name va-va2sp
# README, FORMAT 3: "Each line contains the ID of a VerbAtlas frame F followed by the selectional preferences of the
# roles in F. ... If a role supports multiple selectional preferences, they are separated by a pipe (|). Some frames
# support two types of selectional preferences: Concrete (C) and Abstract (A)."
# What is spoken of is the frame with its type, as the row writes them: [frame, C]. Then a role, and its preferences.
match VA_va2sp.tsv
grammar table
skip 1
columns frame type
list * |

claims
together
subject in frame type
rest pairs
